  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-133306"
  ],
  "description": "It was discovered that libaacs did not properly check buffer bounds when\nresolving symbolic links in Blu-ray disc paths. If a user were tricked into\nopening an attacker-controlled disc directory, a local attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause applications using libaacs to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service, or execute arbitrary code.",
  "id": "USN-9195-1",
  "isummary": "libaacs could be made to crash or run programs if it processed specially\ncrafted symbolic links.",
